# Global fd ignore. Applies to every `fd` invocation, and therefore to
# everything built on it: fzf's Ctrl-T (the omz fzf plugin sets
# FZF_DEFAULT_COMMAND=fd ...), telescope's find_files, and any script
# reaching for fd directly.
#
# These two are rclone FUSE mounts that live *inside* $HOME, so any walk of
# the home directory used to leave the machine and block on the network.
# Measured from ~ before this file existed:
#
#   fd --type f --hidden --exclude .git            41s+ (never finished)
#   ... same, with these two excluded                0.5s
#
# To search inside them deliberately, bypass this file:
#   fd --no-ignore-vcs --no-global-ignore-file <pattern> ~/OneDrive
# or just cd into the mount first, which is unaffected.
OneDrive/
iCloud/
